#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The overview data (#369, sublayer 1e): bin/factory-view prints the data of `factory top`'s state, as the view model of one fresh
# snapshot, JSON on stdout. A page will read it once the Human picks where his one page lives.
# The view model holds, in this order: what waits on the Human, each repository's issues (team, step, pull request with its checks, who it
# waits on), each account's five-hour and weekly use with its teams, and today with the load, each row with its GitHub link and the age of
# the reading.
# Read-only: it writes nothing, starts nothing and reads no credential beyond the gh login that `factory top` already uses. Only the view
# model's fields are in its output (bin/lib/view.mjs, viewOf): no process command line, environment, pid, token path or home path, and an
# account by its letter alone; the raw snapshot never is. Any argument exits 2 with the usage line.
# The page and its hosting wait for the Human's choice (https://github.com/tuannd9288/factory/issues/369#issuecomment-6598838712).
# Run under the Mac mini's `factory` user, it reads only under that home (~/factory-runs, ~/.local/state/factory, the clones), so the macOS
# privacy controls (TCC) that AGENTS.md names for ~/Desktop do not apply.
exec node "$(dirname "$0")/lib/view-cli.mjs" "$@"
